  "notes": "Header labels read from the 40-pin pinout diagram (outer coloured labels as label, inner board silkscreen IOxx as first function). The diagram's 'USB' box is the board's silkscreen orientation mark. The side table maps GPIO0=BOOT Button, GPIO21=BUZZER, GPIO38=RGB, GPIO17=TXD (UART TX to RS485), GPIO18=RXD (UART RX to RS485), GPIO1/2/41/42/45/46=Relay CH1-CH6, VSYS=Power Input; these are not attached to header pins in the drawing so they are not added as pin functions. Skipped: DC 7~36V screw terminal (only +/- marks) and the 18 relay screw terminals (only channel numbers 1-6, no per-terminal labels). Image 2 is the same artwork at a slightly different size; transcribed separately per rule 11."
}